Found while replaying Learn Skills Daily's *InDesign Full Course Tutorial* ([video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BuE8JpajmgY), chapter "Working with Images (Part 2)", 1:11:50–1:12:15). The instructor opens Object › Convert Shape to make a photo's frame round. InDesign's Object menu has a fixed order and grouping; DesignCraft's had the same items in another order (Flex Layout, Paths and Pathfinder near the top, Convert Shape and Select in the middle). Convert Point was missing, and Open/Closed Path were in Convert Shape instead of Paths.

## Change
- **Order:** the Object menu now follows InDesign's order and groups:
  - Transform, Transform Again, Arrange, Select;
  - Group … Show All on Spread;
  - Generate QR Code;
  - Text Frame Options, Primary Text Frame, Anchored Object;
  - Fitting, Content;
  - Effects, Corner Options;
  - Object Layer Options, Object Export Options, Captions, Clipping Path;
  - Flex Layout;
  - Paths, Pathfinder, Convert Shape, Convert Point.

  Flex Layout, from InDesign 2025, isn't in the 2023 menu the video shows, so it has its own group before Paths.
- **Paths:** Join (`path.join`), Open Path, Close Path, Reverse Path, then Make and Release Compound Path.
- **Convert Shape:** only the nine shapes, as InDesign's.
- **Convert Point:** a new submenu with Plain, Corner, Smooth and Symmetrical (`path.convertPoints {kind}`).
- **Not added:** Insert HTML, Image Color Settings, Interactive and Display Performance, which have no commands yet.
- **Translations:** "Join" and "Convert Point" are added to every table; "Plain" and "Symmetrical" to the tables that lacked them (cs, de, ka, pl, ru).

![object menu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moppeeer/designcraft-pr-assets/main/object-menu-order/object_menu_compare.png)

## Test
`the_object_menu_is_in_indesigns_order` checks:
- the top-level order and separators;
- Join, Open Path and Close Path under Paths;
- no open or closed path under Convert Shape;
- the four Convert Point entries.

