Found while replaying Zero2Graphic's *How to Page Layout design (Landscape) in Adobe InDesign 2022 CC* ([video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8PX1tZwOrqI), 4:38–4:53, 6:23–6:32 and 7:11). With several objects selected, InDesign's Properties panel names them by kind: "Mixed Objects" for a number, its text and the square under it, "Text Frames" for the three numbers, and "Linked Files" for the three pictures. DesignCraft always said "Multiple Objects".

![Mixed Objects: InDesign, main and this PR](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moppeeer/designcraft-pr-assets/main/pr-1419/1419-mixed.png)

![Several pictures and one picture placed from a file](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moppeeer/designcraft-pr-assets/main/pr-1419/1419-linked.png)

## Change
- **Title:** with several objects selected, the Properties panel's title is:
  - "Text Frames" when all are text frames;
  - "Linked Files" when all are placed images;
  - "Frames" when all are empty graphic frames, as the slanted row in Zero2Graphic's *How to Page Layout design in Adobe InDesign 2022 CC* ([video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJroNPKnQg8), 2:06);
  - "Mixed Objects" when the kinds differ;
  - "Multiple Objects" otherwise, as before.
- **One picture:** a single picture placed from a file is titled "Linked File", as in the Learn Skills Daily course's chapter 10 ([video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BuE8JpajmgY), 1:13:37). An embedded picture is still titled "Image".
- **Translations:** the five titles are translated in every table.

## Test
`several_objects_are_named_as_indesign_names_them` checks:
- two text frames are titled "Text Frames";
- with a rectangle added, "Mixed Objects";
- one text frame, "Text Frame";
- two empty graphic frames, "Frames", and one of them with a drawn rectangle, "Mixed Objects";
- two placed images, "Linked Files";
- one embedded picture, "Image";
- one picture placed from a file, "Linked File".

The UI tests pass. Clippy and fmt are clean.

## Dependencies
None.

